{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 38,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this that darkeneth counsel by words without knowledge?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gird up now thy loins like a man; for I will demand of thee, and answer thou me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where wast thou when I laid the foundations of the earth? declare, if thou hast understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath laid the measures of it, if thou knowest? or who hath stretched the line upon it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon what are the foundations of it fastened? or who laid its corner stone;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shut up the sea with doors, when it broke forth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it had issued out of the womb?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I made a cloud its garment, and thick darkness a swaddling band for it,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And broke up for it my decreed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and set bars and doors,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, Hitherto shalt thou come, but no further: and here shall thy proud waves be stayed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou commanded the morning since thy days; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " caused the day-spring to know its place;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That it might take hold of the ends of earth, that the wicked might be shaken out of it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is turned as clay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the seal; and they stand as a garment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from the wicked their light is withheld, and the high arm shall be broken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou entered into the springs of the sea? or hast thou walked in the search of the depth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have the gates of death been opened to thee? or hast thou seen the doors of the shades of death?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou perceived the breadth of the earth? declare if thou knowest it all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " light dwelleth? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " darkness, where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its place,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou shouldest take it to its bound, and that thou shouldest know the paths ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its house?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowest thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", because thou wast then born? or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "because",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the number of thy days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which I have reserved against the time of trouble, against the day of battle and war?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By what way is the light parted, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " scattereth the east wind upon the earth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath divided a watercourse for the overflowing of waters, or a way for the lightning of thunder;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To cause it to rain on the earth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wilderness in which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To satisfy the desolate and waste ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ground",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; and to cause the bud of the tender herb to spring forth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hath the rain a father? or who hath begotten the drops of the dew?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Out of whose womb came the ice? and the hoary frost of heaven, who hath gendered it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The waters are hid as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a stone, and the face of the deep is frozen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou bind the sweet influences of Pleiades, or loose the bands of Orion?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou bring forth Mazzaroth in its season? or canst thou guide Arcturus with its sons?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowest thou the ordinances of heaven? canst thou set its dominion on the earth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou lift thy voice to the clouds, that abundance of waters may cover thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou send lightnings, that they may go, and say to thee, Here we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath put wisdom in the inward parts? or who hath given understanding to the heart?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who can number the clouds in wisdom? or who can stay the bottles of heaven,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the dust groweth into hardness, and the clods cleave fast together?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou hunt the prey for the lion? or fill the appetite of the young lions,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When they couch in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dens, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abide in the covert to lie in wait?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.38.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.38.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who provideth for the raven his food? when his young ones cry to God, they wander for want of food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
